project/statichandler-symlink-nodemodules-404: src/sdk/StaticHandler.js's realpath escape-guard (rejects symlinks whose realpath leaves the served mount) 404s file:/workspace/pnpm-linked node_modules packages whose real files live outside the mount by design (e.g. streaming-gltf symlinked to a sibling checkout). An ES-module import of such a package throws on the 404, aborting the importer's (ModelPoolAdapter.js) module graph -> app.js top-level init never runs -> window.__app/__scene/loadingMachine stay undefined and the STATIC HTML click-prompt ('Click to play / press M for multiplayer') sits visible, looking like a stuck singleplayer load on ?singleplayer&world=tps-game. Fix: exempt symlinks whose LEXICAL path contains a node_modules segment from the realpath escape check (the lexical .. containment check above it already blocks attacker-chosen traversal in the request URL). Diagnose via a browser witness capturing failed responses (status>=400) + whether window.* init globals exist, NOT by eyeballing the overlay. test.js has a real-services regression asserting the handler serves a symlinked node_modules path 200.